WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.540
Hold out your hand.

2
00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:04.850
Right now, air molecules
are hitting it, endlessly,

3
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.610
from every direction.

4
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:11.040
There are a very large number of
them, in rapid, random motion.

5
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:15.910
Yet together, those collisions produce
the steady push we call air pressure.

6
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.260
So how fast are those
molecules actually moving?

7
00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:22.240
In this mission, you'll
build the ideal gas model,

8
00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:26.020
and see how pressure comes from
molecules bouncing off a wall.

9
00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.960
Then you'll find out what
temperature really measures,

10
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:33.720
and calculate the root-mean-square
speed of nitrogen at 300 kelvin.

11
00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:38.190
Your mission: find out how fast the
air molecules around you are moving.
